<p>Flooding and landslides after heavy rains in Kenya have killed 18 people, the National Police Service said Sunday, with most deaths attributed to drowning over the past week. Police and interior officials reported flooding and landslides across several regions as sustained rain continued.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/NgFCQ11hGCrA60p0kf5oNOMUdxuZBGthOAVW-5TpVB5rBKSksjpdRAhhbiIWDdLagH_yXV6LiOvH9KBzIdZ11tKWtPtuBjxtydPvp8jl65PWXtZ03bzG5LKpGCtSdxJHWuUnxo_uoPB-fET5tWWnZJCz_Hg-ls-6NripW-M_AQ' alt='Flooding during Kenya’s rainy season, which has turned deadly after heavy rains.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Eastern region: In an earlier police update, officials said the eastern region was hit hardest by the flooding.</li><li>Nairobi response: A local report said Nairobi Governor Sakaja ordered demolitions as heavy rain disrupted the capital.</li><li>Emergency operations: Authorities said search, rescue and evacuation operations were ongoing in affected areas.</li><li>Elgeyo-Marakwet scene: Residents inspected a destroyed homestead after a landslide flattened houses and damaged farmland following days of intense rainfall.</li></ul><blockquote>underscoring the grave danger posed by the ongoing weather conditions - National Police Service</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>National Police Service: The police service called for heightened caution as sustained heavy rainfall increased disaster risks in several regions. (<a href='https://nairobiwire.com/2026/05/kenya-landslides-heavy-rains-deaths-nps-warning.html'>Nairobi Wire</a>)</li><li>Kenya Meteorological Department: The meteorological service warned that the period of heavy rainfall would continue during the first two weeks of May. (<a href='https://www.nrk.no/nyheter/minst-18-personer-dode-i-flom-i-kenya-1.17869983'>NRK</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/kenya-death-toll-from-floods-landslides-rises-to-18-people-police-say'>Kenya death toll from flo